 Ordinary Differential Equations 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

With polynomials of differential operators we can now define ordinary differential equations. 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

An equation of the form 
\begin_inset Formula \[p(D)f=q(D)g\]
\end_inset

 where 
\begin_inset Formula $f,g\in \Cinf$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $p(D),q(D)\in \Real(\Diff)$
\end_inset

, is called an ordinary differential equation with constant coefficients. 
\end_layout

