 Ordinary Differential Equations 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

In 
\begin_inset LatexCommand \eqref{diffeq}

\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $u$
\end_inset

 is ordinarily assumed to be known or given, while 
\begin_inset Formula $y$
\end_inset

 is unknown and sought. 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

Any function 
\begin_inset Formula $y$
\end_inset

 satisfying 
\begin_inset LatexCommand \eqref{diffeq}

\end_inset

 is called a solution of the differential equation. 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

A differential equation such as 
\begin_inset LatexCommand \eqref{diffeq}

\end_inset

 is called 
\shape italic

\series bold
homogeneous
\series default

\shape default
 when the input function 
\begin_inset Formula $u$
\end_inset

 is identically zero for all 
\begin_inset Formula $t\in[a,b]$
\end_inset

. 
\end_layout

