 Ordinary Differential Equations 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

Equation 
\begin_inset LatexCommand \eqref{diffeq}

\end_inset

 
\begin_inset Formula \[\diffeq\]
\end_inset

 is called 
\shape italic

\series bold
time-invariant
\series default

\shape default
, because the coefficients are constant and also because the independent variable 
\begin_inset Formula $t$
\end_inset

 does not appear explicitly in the equation. 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

Note that 
\begin_inset LatexCommand \eqref{diffeq}

\end_inset

 is linear in terms of both the input and the output, because the polynomial differential operator on each side of the equation is a linear operator. 
\end_layout

