\end_layout

\end_inset

 Ordinary Differential Equations 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

In case 1, a fundamental set is easily constructed: 
\begin_inset Formula \[y_1(t)=\exp(r_1t),\ldots,y_n(t)=\exp(r_nt) \]
\end_inset

 where the 
\begin_inset Formula $r_i$
\end_inset

 are the distinct roots. 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

In case 2, each root 
\begin_inset Formula $r_i$
\end_inset

 of multiplicity 
\begin_inset Formula $n_i$
\end_inset

 contributes 
\begin_inset Formula $n_i$
\end_inset

 functions to the fundamental set: 
\begin_inset Formula \[y_{i1}(t)=\exp(r_it),y_{i2}(t)=t\exp(r_it),\ldots,y_{in_i}(t)=t^{n_i-1}\exp(r_it) \]
\end_inset

 
\end_layout

