 Ordinary Differential Equations 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

To fully solve the differential equation, the initial conditions need to be taken into account. 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

These are the values of the function and its first 
\begin_inset Formula $n-1$
\end_inset

 derivatives at the start of the time interval. 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

We will specialize our interval 
\begin_inset Formula $[a,b]$
\end_inset

 to the case in which 
\begin_inset Formula $a=0$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $b=T$
\end_inset

, some unspecified time in the future. 
\end_layout

