 Ordinary Differential Equations 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

The 
\shape italic

\series bold
free response
\series default

\shape default
 is the solution to the homogeneous equation in which the initial conditions are specified but the input is zero, i.e., there is no forcing function.: 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation}\label{initcond}
  y(0),Dy(0),\ldots,D^{n-1}y(0)
\end{equation}
\end_inset

 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

The 
\shape italic

\series bold
forced response
\series default

\shape default
 reverses this situation; it allows the input function to be non-zero, but it requires all the initial conditions in 
\begin_inset LatexCommand \eqref{initcond}

\end_inset

 to be zero. 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

The 
\shape italic

\series bold
total response
\series default

\shape default
 is the sum of the free and forced responses. 
\end_layout

