 Ordinary Differential Equations: Example of Free, Forced and Total Responses 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

Consider 
\begin_inset Formula $D^2y+3Dy-1y=u$
\end_inset

 with initial conditions: 
\begin_inset Formula $y(0)=1,Dy(0)=-1$
\end_inset

. 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

The roots (found using Matlab's roots function) are 
\begin_inset Formula $r_1=-3.3028$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $r_2=0.3028$
\end_inset

, and they are distinct. 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

Therefore, a fundamental set is 
\begin_inset Formula $\set{\exp(-3.3028t),\exp(0.3028t)}$
\end_inset

. 
\end_layout

